  <running_head>De Nono Præcepto</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">nacia in errore semel-coepto. 2 Thess.</l>
    <l n="2">2. v. 10. seq.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">Candor est, quo bona in quoque</l>
    <l n="4">sincere agnoscuntur; aliorum &amp; dicta &amp; facta,</l>
    <l n="5">ambigua præsertim, in meliorem partem</l>
    <l n="6">exponuntur. 1 Cor. 13 v.6.7. Tit.3.v.2.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">Illi adversatur: Temeritas in damnando,</l>
    <l n="8">Matt.7.v.1. Dolus malus in aliorum dictis</l>
    <l n="9">&amp; factis depravandis, Matt.26.v 60. Cu-</l>
    <l n="10">riositas in arcanis aliorum scrutandis, atq;</l>
    <l n="11">Futilitas in iisdem evulgandis: Prov.11.v.13.</l>
    <l n="12">itemq; Adulatio, Prov.27. v.14. Roman. 16.v.18.</l>
    <l n="13" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Hactenus quomodo proximi boni</l>
    <l n="14" type="heading" level="2">promovendi facto studere</l>
    <l n="15" type="heading" level="2">debeamus.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">Decimo demum præcepto: affectuum</l>
    <l n="17">rectitudo sancitur; pravæq; cupiditates</l>
    <l n="18">inhibentur.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">Affectuum q: facultatis, cum appe-</l>
    <l n="20">tentis, tum iracentis.</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">Appetentis sunt: Gaudium, Spes,</l>
    <l n="22">&amp; Amor; in bonis: contra, Mœstitia,</l>
    <l n="23">Metus, atq; Odium; in malis. Rom.13.</l>
    <l n="24">v.14. Eph.4.v.23. 1 Thess.5.v.23. 1 Tim.1.v.5;</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Prohibentur ergo hic; Ἀπιχαιρεκακία.</l>
    <l n="26" type="foot" para="true">Ε</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The Greek word at the end of the page is partly illegible in the scan; the transcription of "Ἀπιχαιρεκακία" is approximate. The letter at the foot is a signature-like mark, given as printed. Some marginal-looking show-through from the reverse side was ignored.</notes>
</page>
